---
description: Catalan full female name — one given name and TWO surnames, paternal then maternal, joined by the connector "i" in the formal Catalan style (Montserrat Roig i Fransitorra, Merce Rodoreda i Gurgui, Caterina Albert i Paradis). A Catalan woman keeps her own two surnames for life and never takes her husband's, so this generator is the same shape as the male one. Catalan surnames do not inflect for gender — there is no -ska/-ova change and no person/female/lastName.txt in this pack — so both surnames come from the single person.lastName list. The Spanish civil registry writes the same name without the "i".
generator: tdc
locale: ca
---
<sequence name="p">
  <gen name="f" type="template" value="ca.person.female.firstName"/>
  <distinct>
    <gen name="l1" type="template" value="ca.person.lastName"/>
    <gen name="l2" type="template" value="ca.person.lastName"/>
  </distinct>
</sequence>
<data>${{p.f}} ${{p.l1}} i ${{p.l2}}</data>
